cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its harmonized data, please cite it as below, and cite NASA FIRMS for the source detections (see DATA_LICENSE.md)."
title: "Burning calendar: harmonized MODIS + VIIRS fire hotspots for Greece and Argentina"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Petr
    family-names: Mikeska
  - given-names: Vít
    family-names: Kadlec
version: v1
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MetrPikeska/burning-calendar"
url: "https://burning-calendar.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Monthly active fire detection counts from MODIS (Terra and Aqua, from Nov 2000)
  and VIIRS S-NPP 375 m (from 2012) joined into one VIIRS-equivalent series per
  region for Greek NUTS2 regions and Argentine provinces, Nov 2000 to Dec 2025.
  Method version v1-region-month-dn-loyo: factors per region, month and day/night
  fitted on 2012-2019, leave-one-year-out validation, back-cast intervals for
  months before 2012. Built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (CONAE challenge
  "Harmonization of MODIS and VIIRS Hot Spots").
keywords:
  - active fire
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - FIRMS
  - harmonization
  - Greece
  - Argentina
